  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response to the impact of flooding in the Dadaab refugee camps, in Garissa County</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main aim of this UNHCR project is to provide emergency NFIs and shelter to refugees affected by flooding in Dadaab. UNHCR and partners procures and distributes non-food items (NFIs) and shelter kits to 250 targeted households, including vulnerable refugees and persons with disabilities. Additionally, UNHCR procures and disinfects 250 latrines. To mitigate the spread of waterborne diseases, hygiene awareness information is disseminated. In total, the project targets 23,000 people, including 5,100 women and 5,000 men,13,000 children and approximately 1,250 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
